WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.600
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:05.315 --> 01:06.191
Hey.

01:08.735 --> 01:09.611
Stop right there.

01:10.403 --> 01:11.237
Hey!

01:18.286 --> 01:20.246
[Seok-ryu breathing heavily]

01:24.959 --> 01:26.961
[mellow music playing]

01:30.340 --> 01:31.674
What you said earlier…

01:34.594 --> 01:35.887
what did you mean?

02:15.802 --> 02:16.886
[man] Seok-ryu.

02:23.309 --> 02:24.394
Hyeon-jun?

02:27.438 --> 02:28.982
What are you doing here?

02:29.899 --> 02:32.819
I got on a plane to see you.

02:34.487 --> 02:35.780
I've missed you.

02:40.535 --> 02:41.578
What are you doing?

02:42.954 --> 02:44.706
Can't you see I'm talking with her?

02:46.958 --> 02:48.751
I know you.

02:48.835 --> 02:52.630
You're Choi Seung-hyo, right?
Seok-ryu's childhood friend.

02:54.424 --> 02:56.301
I think you know me too.

02:56.801 --> 02:58.928
It's nice to meet you. I'm Song Hyeon-jun.

03:00.597 --> 03:02.056
I can't say the same.

03:03.224 --> 03:05.351
We're not on greeting terms either.

03:05.935 --> 03:07.437
Oh, is that so?

03:07.520 --> 03:09.606
Why did you even show up here?

03:11.107 --> 03:13.067
And why now of all times?

03:15.653 --> 03:18.156
Why, what was going on?

03:18.239 --> 03:20.450
I don't think I need to
give you an answer.

03:23.161 --> 03:24.078
Let's go, Seok-ryu.

03:24.704 --> 03:26.372
-Hey.
-I have something to say.

03:26.956 --> 03:27.916
A lot too.

03:27.999 --> 03:29.792
[Geun-sik] What do you think you're doing?

03:31.711 --> 03:34.047
-Sir. Ma'am.
-What the hell are you doing?

03:35.798 --> 03:38.051
How dare you come here?

03:39.260 --> 03:40.220
Let go.

03:41.137 --> 03:41.971
Let go of me.

03:42.722 --> 03:44.474
Mi-suk, don't try to stop me.

03:44.557 --> 03:47.227
Even if it kills me,
I'm going to destroy this bastard tonight!

03:47.310 --> 03:48.478
[Mi-suk] I won't stop you.

03:48.978 --> 03:51.189
But you can't do it here.

03:52.148 --> 03:53.775
One neighborhood commotion is enough.

03:55.735 --> 03:57.445
[breath trembling]

04:01.908 --> 04:03.368
You bastard… [sighs]

04:05.161 --> 04:07.455
[exhales deeply]

04:12.252 --> 04:14.420
[Mi-suk] Are you coming home
from work, Seung-hyo?

04:14.504 --> 04:15.797
Yeah.

04:15.880 --> 04:17.757
Well done.
I'm sure you're tired. Go on home.

04:19.384 --> 04:22.011
And Seok-ryu, you come home.

04:24.847 --> 04:26.015
You too, Hyeon-jun.

04:27.433 --> 04:29.894
[Seok-ryu] Mom,
why would you invite him home?

04:30.603 --> 04:32.855
This is between us.

04:32.939 --> 04:34.399
I'll take care of it.

04:34.482 --> 04:37.360
It's a family matter. There should be
etiquette in relationships too.

04:37.443 --> 04:39.612
You two called things off
without our consent!

04:41.572 --> 04:42.824
Is marriage a game?

04:44.617 --> 04:46.286
Enough talking. You two come with me.

04:56.379 --> 04:57.714
[exhales]

05:00.216 --> 05:01.217
[smacks lips]

05:05.805 --> 05:08.516
-[Mi-suk] Do you want more food?
-[Hyeon-jun] Yes, please.

05:09.642 --> 05:11.769
-[Geun-sik exhales]
-Why is Mom so calm?

05:11.853 --> 05:13.021
Why is she being so generous?

05:13.896 --> 05:16.232
She's possessed by a ghost
who can't let people starve.

05:18.776 --> 05:20.528
Jeez, do I need to call a shaman?

05:21.029 --> 05:24.407
Then, what about my brother-in-law?
Was he always this shameless?

05:24.490 --> 05:27.285
-Brother-in-law? Don't call him that.
-[grunts]

05:27.368 --> 05:31.247
I thought he was just trying
to be friendly then.

05:32.373 --> 05:33.458
Was it two years ago?

05:33.541 --> 05:36.502
He came to our house for vacation
because Seok-ryu was busy.

05:37.295 --> 05:38.463
Oh, right.

05:39.047 --> 05:41.007
He gave me a bunch
of pocket money back then.

05:41.090 --> 05:42.884
Shut your mouth.

05:43.634 --> 05:44.886
[Mi-suk] Do you want more soup?

05:46.471 --> 05:47.638
Yes, I'd appreciate it.

05:47.722 --> 05:49.640
[Geun-sik scoffs] My goodness.

05:49.724 --> 05:51.434
He doesn't know when to refuse, does he?

05:51.517 --> 05:52.769
That little punk.

05:54.062 --> 05:55.146
Goodness.

05:55.772 --> 05:57.940
-Dad, where are you going?
-[Geun-sik] The rooftop.

05:58.024 --> 06:01.444
I can't stand being
in the same room as that bastard!

06:02.028 --> 06:03.529
Just give him everything!

06:03.613 --> 06:05.156
Just eat until you explode!

06:08.701 --> 06:09.535
[door closes]

06:09.619 --> 06:11.913
-Yeah, eat up.
-Thank you.

06:13.915 --> 06:15.374
[quirky music playing]

06:15.458 --> 06:16.667
My head hurts.

06:18.836 --> 06:19.670
[exhales]

06:25.259 --> 06:26.177
[Seung-hyo scoffs]

06:27.470 --> 06:30.765
Hey, why aren't you going in?
Aren't you here to see Seok-ryu?

06:32.016 --> 06:34.852
Forget it.
There's an unwelcome guest inside.

06:35.436 --> 06:37.522
Unwelcome guest? Who?

06:38.523 --> 06:39.982
Seok-ryu's ex-fiancé.

06:40.066 --> 06:41.067
What?

06:42.318 --> 06:44.362
Is this bastard high?

06:44.445 --> 06:47.073
How dare he appear in front of Seok-ryu?

06:47.156 --> 06:47.990
I'll kill him.

06:48.741 --> 06:49.909
Don't do anything.

06:49.992 --> 06:52.495
Why? We have to kill that jerk.

06:53.079 --> 06:54.622
I want to kill him more.

07:03.381 --> 07:04.423
[Mi-suk sighs]

07:10.972 --> 07:14.142
Did you get enough to eat?

07:14.225 --> 07:17.728
Yes, it was delicious. Thank you.

07:17.812 --> 07:18.813
That's good.

07:20.231 --> 07:23.901
I feel like I've done my duty,
so I'll say what's on my mind now.

07:23.985 --> 07:27.196
Mom, why are you talking like that?
Are you shooting a historical drama?

07:31.242 --> 07:32.201
From what I hear,

07:33.578 --> 07:36.330
Seok-ryu cheated on you. Is that true?

07:37.582 --> 07:38.416
Excuse me?

07:38.499 --> 07:40.668
No, of course not…

07:43.087 --> 07:44.088
Unless you did?

07:44.172 --> 07:45.047
[sighs]

07:48.134 --> 07:49.260
Then…

07:49.886 --> 07:51.262
did you cheat?

07:51.345 --> 07:52.805
No, I didn't.

07:55.141 --> 07:56.809
But it was my fault.

07:58.144 --> 08:01.189
I take full responsibility
for breaking off our engagement.

08:01.272 --> 08:03.483
-[sighs]
-You little punk!

08:03.566 --> 08:05.067
[Seok-ryu] Dad, don't!

08:05.151 --> 08:06.486
Hyeon-jun, that's enough.

08:07.945 --> 08:09.322
It's not like that, Mom.

08:09.405 --> 08:10.615
[exhales]

08:11.991 --> 08:14.619
I had a feeling my daughter
wouldn't have done that.

08:15.369 --> 08:17.788
Still, I wanted to ask to make sure.

08:17.872 --> 08:20.458
If it were true, I wanted to apologize.

08:21.083 --> 08:22.293
But since that's not the case…

08:23.836 --> 08:24.921
You bastard.

08:25.588 --> 08:26.506
Come get this beating.

08:26.589 --> 08:28.049
-Wait, honey.
-[Seok-ryu] Mom!

08:28.132 --> 08:31.219
-Mi-suk!
-Mom! I said it wasn't his fault.

08:31.302 --> 08:33.554
You can't hit people with this!
You'll kill him!

08:33.638 --> 08:35.473
Fine. I'll kill this bastard
and go to jail.

08:35.556 --> 08:37.225
Hey, you bastard!

08:37.308 --> 08:39.143
How dare you break my daughter's heart?

08:39.227 --> 08:40.311
How dare you?

08:40.394 --> 08:43.439
-I told you I can't go to jail with you!
-Mom, please!

08:44.607 --> 08:45.858
Hyeon-jun, let's go.

08:45.942 --> 08:47.068
I've seen this before.

08:47.151 --> 08:48.945
It's totally déjà vu.
This is so immersive!

08:49.028 --> 08:51.072
-[Seok-ryu] Come on.
-Hit me until you feel better!

08:51.155 --> 08:52.240
That's why I came here.

08:52.323 --> 08:54.367
-You're going to die.
-Good.

08:54.450 --> 08:55.618
You think I won't?

08:55.701 --> 08:57.370
Mom! Jeez!

08:57.453 --> 08:59.163
-Mom, stop!
-[Geun-sik] Not too much!

08:59.247 --> 09:01.082
Wow! This woman's so strong!

09:01.165 --> 09:03.584
[Seok-ryu] Come on. I said let's go!

09:03.668 --> 09:05.127
Come on.

09:05.211 --> 09:06.879
Ma'am, I'm sorry.

09:06.963 --> 09:09.840
You punk! I can't let that bastard
leave in one piece!

09:09.924 --> 09:11.968
I'll come back again, sir.

09:12.051 --> 09:13.928
Don't come ever come back, you bastard!

09:14.011 --> 09:15.721
If I ever see you here again,

09:15.805 --> 09:18.057
I'll knock your head off, you prick!

09:18.140 --> 09:20.476
My son works out, punk!

09:22.144 --> 09:23.271
[groans]

09:23.771 --> 09:27.358
This burning sense of justice
is rising from my core.

09:27.900 --> 09:29.652
Beer's not enough to cool it.

09:30.778 --> 09:31.988
Want another one?

09:32.071 --> 09:34.949
Let's go and cause a scene instead.
I'll cover the costs.

09:35.032 --> 09:37.159
Whatever.
You won't even pay for the beer.

09:38.202 --> 09:39.954
You said you wanted to
kill him even more.

09:40.037 --> 09:41.247
I was just saying.

09:41.330 --> 09:42.540
-Who am I to do that?
-What?

09:43.958 --> 09:45.501
What do you mean?

09:45.585 --> 09:48.879
You're the son of Seok-ryu's mom's friend.

09:48.963 --> 09:51.549
You've been her best friend
since childhood.

09:52.133 --> 09:53.092
Exactly.

09:54.051 --> 09:56.137
-We're just friends.
-Hey!

09:56.220 --> 09:58.556
Being friends is an incredible thing.

09:58.639 --> 10:03.185
One definition of a friend says it's one
who carries my sorrows on their back.

10:03.978 --> 10:05.146
How cool is that?

10:05.229 --> 10:08.524
What if I get involved
and dig up more of her sorrows?

10:08.608 --> 10:11.027
-I don't even know how she feels.
-[Mo-eum scoffs]

10:11.110 --> 10:14.322
You're so frustrating.
How much longer will you keep this up?

10:14.905 --> 10:16.991
When I think of all the time
you've wasted already,

10:17.950 --> 10:21.037
you could've dug
until you reached the Earth's core.

10:21.120 --> 10:22.371
[mellow music playing]

10:22.455 --> 10:23.873
Mo-eum, did you…

10:23.956 --> 10:26.751
That's right. I saw the time capsule.

10:27.835 --> 10:31.005
Hey. You should've buried just the letter.

10:31.088 --> 10:33.424
If you hide your feelings in there too,

10:34.091 --> 10:35.551
how would anyone know?

10:36.510 --> 10:37.887
-Look.
-[Seung-hyo clears throat]

10:37.970 --> 10:40.598
You're the only one who's suffering.

10:40.681 --> 10:43.893
You didn't tell her, did you?

10:43.976 --> 10:44.810
Are you insane?

10:45.978 --> 10:49.231
Seung-hyo, you have to
save yourself from unrequited love.

10:49.315 --> 10:50.691
Even I can't rescue you.

10:53.527 --> 10:54.820
-[sighs]
-[Mo-eum] But…

10:57.073 --> 10:58.407
I will root for you.

10:59.909 --> 11:00.868
[slurps]

11:03.120 --> 11:03.954
I'm off.

11:04.038 --> 11:05.039
[grunts]

11:06.499 --> 11:09.543
Darn, I should've teased him
about it some more.

11:09.627 --> 11:10.670
[chuckles softly]

11:14.256 --> 11:15.257
[smacks lips]

11:20.638 --> 11:21.597
[slurps]

11:22.515 --> 11:23.391
[crushes can]

11:25.309 --> 11:31.607
LOVE IS ALL ABOUT TIMING

11:32.691 --> 11:34.777
[lounge music playing in the background]

11:38.030 --> 11:39.490
Why did you come?

11:41.075 --> 11:43.744
Did you come to be beaten to death
by my parents?

11:43.828 --> 11:46.247
No, I came to live.

11:47.331 --> 11:50.584
I came because I wanted to
breathe, eat, and sleep again.

11:52.086 --> 11:54.380
-[sighs]
-[Hyeon-jun] Without you,

11:55.840 --> 11:58.551
I can't do those basic things.
I can't live.

11:58.634 --> 12:00.136
That's not because of me.

12:00.970 --> 12:03.055
It wasn't because we were special either.

12:05.099 --> 12:07.309
It would've been the same with anyone.

12:08.602 --> 12:09.979
We dated for years.

12:10.062 --> 12:12.314
-It's an obvious feeling.
-Don't say that.

12:13.607 --> 12:15.317
No matter how much you hate me,

12:15.985 --> 12:18.362
don't say it as if we were nothing.

12:20.197 --> 12:21.866
-Seok-ryu…
-[Seok-ryu exhales]

12:21.949 --> 12:23.534
I came to get you back.

12:25.786 --> 12:26.871
I still love you.

12:28.747 --> 12:31.459
Hyeon-jun, it's over between us.

12:32.751 --> 12:34.211
It's not love you feel anymore.

12:35.880 --> 12:36.922
It's just a habit.

12:37.882 --> 12:39.717
A bad habit you've yet to fix.

12:43.637 --> 12:47.224
Don't come back here. Please.

13:03.032 --> 13:04.825
I'm sleeping over. Give me some clothes.

13:04.909 --> 13:06.076
[Mo-eum] What?

13:07.077 --> 13:08.078
My goodness.

13:08.954 --> 13:10.873
-Did you run away from home?
-Probably.

13:11.457 --> 13:15.711
I bet it was interesting to see
Hyeon-jun inside your house.

13:15.794 --> 13:17.004
How did you know?

13:17.087 --> 13:18.130
I ran into Seung-hyo.

13:18.214 --> 13:20.382
-You did? Where?
-In front of your house.

13:20.466 --> 13:22.134
He was pacing back and forth,

13:22.218 --> 13:23.511
like a dog that needed to pee.

13:23.594 --> 13:26.555
[Jae-suk] Mo-eum! Come here.

13:26.639 --> 13:28.974
Jeez, why now? In a bit!

13:29.058 --> 13:32.436
[Jae-suk] Hey, my carpal tunnel
or whatever is hurting my wrist,

13:32.520 --> 13:35.189
-so I can't open this jar of jam!
-Jeez.

13:35.272 --> 13:38.150
Hold on! Hey, give me a second.
I need to help my mom.

13:38.234 --> 13:39.944
-I'll be right back.
-[Seok-ryu] Sure.

13:40.027 --> 13:41.987
[Mo-eum] Mom, I told you
if you eat that at night,

13:42.071 --> 13:43.489
your blood sugar will spike!

13:43.572 --> 13:44.573
[footsteps descending]

13:56.377 --> 13:58.379
[inhales, exhales]

14:00.297 --> 14:01.131
Are you asleep?

14:02.383 --> 14:03.384
No.

14:04.176 --> 14:05.094
[Mo-eum] Okay.

14:06.512 --> 14:07.429
Are you sleepy?

14:07.513 --> 14:08.639
[chuckles]

14:08.722 --> 14:11.267
No, say what you want to say.

14:12.560 --> 14:14.603
How does it feel to see Hyeon-jun again?

14:14.687 --> 14:15.729
[scoffs]

14:15.813 --> 14:17.064
Took you long enough.

14:17.648 --> 14:18.649
I mean,

14:19.984 --> 14:23.362
I just remembered
what we talked about last time.

14:24.321 --> 14:26.740
Don't eat until I get back. Wait for me.

14:26.824 --> 14:28.158
Don't you dare lay a finger.

14:30.202 --> 14:31.787
[mellow music playing]

14:35.165 --> 14:36.125
[Mo-eum] Hey.

14:36.709 --> 14:38.168
You still love him?

14:39.587 --> 14:42.590
-Your ex?
-That's half-right and half-wrong.

14:44.508 --> 14:46.093
What does that mean?

14:47.177 --> 14:50.097
I loved the time we spent together.

14:51.056 --> 14:53.309
Everything he gave me.

14:53.893 --> 14:55.185
I still love that.

14:56.604 --> 14:58.564
But for some relationships,

14:59.148 --> 15:01.150
I know it's better to end them.

15:02.818 --> 15:04.737
So I'm doing my best to forget him.

15:05.279 --> 15:06.697
And he needs to do the same.

15:08.616 --> 15:12.369
Has there been
any changes in your feelings since then?

15:13.370 --> 15:16.665
Nope. I'm much more calmer
than I thought I'd be.

15:17.666 --> 15:20.669
Even when I was getting on
the flight for Korea,

15:20.753 --> 15:23.047
just the thought of seeing him again

15:24.298 --> 15:26.508
made my heart feel like it would burst.

15:26.592 --> 15:28.552
[exhales] Okay.

15:28.636 --> 15:31.972
Well then, I guess there's no need
for me to get involved, right?

15:32.556 --> 15:33.390
[Seok-ryu] What?

15:33.474 --> 15:34.516
I mean,

15:34.600 --> 15:36.894
if you wanted,
I was going to beat him up for you.

15:37.478 --> 15:39.396
I would've waited right behind you.

15:39.480 --> 15:41.273
As long as I don't kill him, it'd be fine.

15:41.357 --> 15:45.903
[chuckles] Hey, isn't it illegal
to aid and abet in assault?

15:45.986 --> 15:47.529
[chuckles]

15:47.613 --> 15:50.908
Look, a true hero

15:51.450 --> 15:54.620
can put aside their lifetime job
in the name of friendship.

15:54.703 --> 15:57.748
Forget it. [chuckles]
Just worry about your civil service job.

15:57.831 --> 16:00.668
Your wish is my command.

16:02.086 --> 16:02.920
[inhales]

16:03.003 --> 16:06.507
All right. To ensure the safety
of our citizens tomorrow,

16:06.590 --> 16:08.092
I shall proceed to sleep.

16:09.009 --> 16:10.094
Good night.

16:11.720 --> 16:15.391
Don't fight for world peace
in your dreams and get some rest.

16:15.474 --> 16:18.268
[chuckling] Okay, I'll try.

16:20.145 --> 16:21.146
Goodness.

16:21.897 --> 16:23.023
Still, I'm relieved.

16:24.775 --> 16:27.987
It seems your feelings have dulled a bit.

16:29.863 --> 16:30.906
The feelings for your ex.

16:30.990 --> 16:32.533
[mellow music playing]

16:37.287 --> 16:38.539
[Seung-hyo sighs]

16:49.091 --> 16:52.302
BAE SEOK-RYU

16:57.683 --> 17:00.102
CHOISSEUNG

17:16.618 --> 17:17.870
[birds chirping]

17:19.955 --> 17:20.873
[Geun-sik] Honey?

17:25.544 --> 17:27.129
Honey, it's time for breakfast.

17:28.589 --> 17:30.382
You want me to kill you this early?

17:31.091 --> 17:32.509
You expect me to make breakfast?

17:33.260 --> 17:34.636
No, come and eat.

17:43.437 --> 17:45.272
Why did you make
tteokbokki for breakfast?

17:45.355 --> 17:48.108
Spicy food is the perfect remedy
for stress.

17:48.734 --> 17:53.697
Experience the privilege of being the wife
of a tteokbokki shop owner. [chuckles]

17:54.323 --> 17:57.910
Yeah, it's better to have
my stomach hurt than my heart.

17:59.578 --> 18:01.455
By the way, did Seok-ryu come home?

18:02.331 --> 18:03.791
I think she's in her room.

18:05.375 --> 18:06.543
Speaking of which,

18:07.586 --> 18:11.423
do you think she was trying to protect him
by taking him out like that?

18:11.507 --> 18:12.508
What are you saying?

18:13.759 --> 18:15.427
He was about to get knocked out,

18:15.511 --> 18:18.931
so she took him out of the ring
before you could land a haymaker.

18:19.014 --> 18:20.599
In any case… [chuckles]

18:21.308 --> 18:23.519
…it's as if you were Mike Tyson
or Manny Pacquiao.

18:23.602 --> 18:25.771
You went wild on him. [chuckles]

18:28.065 --> 18:28.899
You did great.

18:30.442 --> 18:33.862
It made me feel better
to see you hit that punk like that.

18:34.822 --> 18:35.823
God.

18:36.448 --> 18:38.659
Maybe I shouldn't have hit him though.

18:39.243 --> 18:41.036
-[Geun-sik] What?
-You know.

18:41.120 --> 18:43.205
You think he came here to get hit?

18:43.288 --> 18:46.750
-He must still have feelings for her.
-What are you trying to say?

18:46.834 --> 18:49.586
I know it's late, but if they want to,

18:49.670 --> 18:51.630
I'd be okay if they got back together.

18:53.132 --> 18:56.135
Her life will return to normal
if she goes back to the US with him.

18:56.218 --> 18:58.053
You think that makes any sense?

18:58.137 --> 18:59.138
Come on, why not?

18:59.221 --> 19:01.849
A person's feelings
aren't always logical or consistent.

19:01.932 --> 19:02.933
No!

19:03.600 --> 19:05.227
What are you… Absolutely not!

19:06.645 --> 19:11.108
That punk hurt Seok-ryu. I hate him.
And I don't want her to go to the US!

19:12.192 --> 19:15.320
I mean… I don't want it either…

19:19.366 --> 19:20.784
I'll give you some fish cake broth.

19:21.785 --> 19:24.204
-It'll be refreshing.
-[phone vibrating]

19:25.080 --> 19:26.206
[clicks tongue]

19:32.212 --> 19:36.008
KOREAN FOOD CRAFTSMAN
PRACTICAL SKILLS

19:41.138 --> 19:43.724
JIJIM NUREUMJEOK

19:43.807 --> 19:46.310
Choisseung didn't even get taste this.

19:46.977 --> 19:48.896
[Mi-suk] Seok-ryu!

19:51.440 --> 19:53.734
-Mom, please knock.
-Where are you going?

19:54.318 --> 19:55.611
I have plans.

19:55.694 --> 19:57.696
You're going out dressed like that?

19:57.779 --> 19:59.031
Yeah. Why?

19:59.615 --> 20:01.033
Get changed. Wear something else.

20:01.116 --> 20:02.326
Why? I don't want to.

20:02.409 --> 20:04.203
Don't embarrass me
in front of our neighbors!

20:04.286 --> 20:06.872
You always walk around
in worn-out T-shirts and flip-flops.

20:06.955 --> 20:08.916
They can tell you're unemployed
from a mile away.

20:08.999 --> 20:11.043
-Because I am.
-[Mi-suk] You little brat!

20:11.126 --> 20:13.045
You want me to wear a dress then?

20:13.128 --> 20:14.421
This is nice. A dress.

20:15.297 --> 20:18.300
Who'd wear this around the neighborhood?

20:18.383 --> 20:22.971
You. Look at those bags under your eyes.
And why are your lips so pale?

20:23.055 --> 20:25.474
-Did you even wash your face?
-Seriously?

20:26.225 --> 20:27.434
[Mi-suk] Look at me.

20:27.976 --> 20:29.561
You look so lifeless.

20:29.645 --> 20:30.938
Are you aging now?

20:31.521 --> 20:33.232
Put some makeup on.

20:33.315 --> 20:35.692
-[Seok-ryu] What's with you?
-Add a little blush too.

20:37.486 --> 20:39.154
Apply some red lipstick.

20:40.948 --> 20:42.950
What's suddenly gotten into her?

20:45.327 --> 20:48.413
Who goes to class dressed like this?

20:59.174 --> 21:00.467
You look pretty today.

21:01.009 --> 21:02.511
[quirky music playing]

21:05.222 --> 21:06.640
[chuckles softly]

21:07.015 --> 21:08.725
I'LL BE THERE SOON
I HAVE SOMETHING TO SAY

21:08.809 --> 21:12.354
You need rocks to smack
into each other to see if sparks will fly.

21:14.690 --> 21:16.900
I guess Mom had an ulterior motive.

21:17.484 --> 21:18.402
[Hyeon-jun] What?

21:18.485 --> 21:19.695
It's nothing.

21:20.237 --> 21:21.863
What brings you here?

21:21.947 --> 21:23.991
I clearly told you not to come back.

21:24.658 --> 21:26.285
I told you I came back for you.

21:26.368 --> 21:27.369
[door opens]

21:33.375 --> 21:34.251
So we meet again.

21:34.334 --> 21:35.460
[sighs softly]

21:35.544 --> 21:36.378
Come on. Get on.

21:36.461 --> 21:38.130
-What?
-Aren't you going to class?

21:38.213 --> 21:39.339
You'll be late.

21:39.423 --> 21:40.799
That's right.

21:41.925 --> 21:42.843
Seok-ryu.

21:45.178 --> 21:46.013
Grab on tight.

21:47.180 --> 21:48.307
[pop song playing]

22:04.781 --> 22:05.949
What's with the bike?

22:06.908 --> 22:08.410
The Earth is sick.

22:08.493 --> 22:11.663
It's an environmentally-friendly approach
for an architect who's concerned

22:11.747 --> 22:13.915
about the climate crisis
and carbon neutrality.

22:13.999 --> 22:16.585
Also, the extra weight
makes for a good workout.

22:16.668 --> 22:18.295
You told me to get on.

22:19.421 --> 22:21.548
What's with the dress?
It doesn't suit you.

22:21.631 --> 22:23.884
-And what did you do to your cheeks?
-Hey.

22:23.967 --> 22:26.636
If you're talking about my blush,

22:26.720 --> 22:29.139
it's Peach Fuzz,
and it's this year's color of the year.

22:29.222 --> 22:30.307
As if you knew!

22:30.390 --> 22:33.560
Goodness, I guess
you were expecting to run into him

22:33.643 --> 22:35.145
since you're dressed up like this.

22:35.228 --> 22:36.229
That's not true!

22:37.064 --> 22:38.774
This was my mom's doing.

22:40.067 --> 22:42.277
I'm not going to eat
her side dishes anymore.

22:42.360 --> 22:44.279
I can't hear you. What was that?

22:45.155 --> 22:46.740
I said you look ugly.

22:48.241 --> 22:50.577
I couldn't hear you again.
Can you repeat that?

22:51.661 --> 22:53.288
You look ugly-- [exclaims]

22:53.872 --> 22:57.167
Hey! That's dangerous. We could crash!

22:57.250 --> 22:59.086
Then, stop messing around!

22:59.169 --> 23:01.630
Jeez, what a lunatic.

23:03.590 --> 23:05.342
[song continues playing]

23:37.082 --> 23:38.834
-Last night--
-About last night--

23:40.127 --> 23:41.711
-Go ahead.
-No, you first.

23:41.795 --> 23:43.255
No, you go.

23:44.589 --> 23:45.549
[gulps]

23:45.632 --> 23:47.843
What did he say last night?

23:48.426 --> 23:49.427
What?

23:49.511 --> 23:52.639
He wouldn't have come here
from the US because he was bored.

23:53.223 --> 23:54.975
He must have come for a reason.

23:57.435 --> 23:58.436
Don't tell me…

23:59.813 --> 24:01.481
-Does he want to get back together?
-What?

24:02.315 --> 24:03.733
Well…

24:05.402 --> 24:07.445
Well, so…

24:08.321 --> 24:09.322
I must be right.

24:10.115 --> 24:12.492
What? Did you start to waver
after hearing that?

24:13.493 --> 24:14.494
[sighs softly]

24:15.662 --> 24:16.580
I don't blame you.

24:17.414 --> 24:19.791
It must've felt nice again
to see him after so long.

24:19.875 --> 24:22.878
Hey, is that the only way you can talk?

24:22.961 --> 24:26.089
It's true.
It's not like you two were just dating.

24:27.048 --> 24:28.216
You were engaged.

24:28.300 --> 24:29.467
Seung-hyo!

24:29.551 --> 24:30.760
Still,

24:30.844 --> 24:32.721
how could you be swayed by that?

24:32.804 --> 24:34.598
Don't you have any self-respect?

24:34.681 --> 24:36.099
Stop the bike.

24:37.350 --> 24:39.186
-I said stop!
-Damn it.

24:39.269 --> 24:40.145
[grunts]

24:41.938 --> 24:44.357
-[quirky music playing]
-[sighs]

24:46.818 --> 24:47.694
You said stop.

24:48.236 --> 24:49.487
Jerk.

24:49.571 --> 24:50.614
[Seung-hyo exclaims]

24:51.656 --> 24:52.657
Hey.

24:55.869 --> 24:56.786
[groans softly]

25:02.792 --> 25:03.793
[sighs]

25:06.254 --> 25:08.089
[slicing]

25:16.973 --> 25:19.309
What is it? Did I do something wrong?

25:19.392 --> 25:20.727
[chuckling] No.

25:20.810 --> 25:23.521
You look full of energy today.

25:24.189 --> 25:25.815
-You can do it.
-I can do it.

25:40.580 --> 25:41.414
[door closes]

25:43.166 --> 25:45.919
-Hey, Seung-hyo. Want some coffee?
-Should I make some for you?

25:46.002 --> 25:48.463
[Seung-hyo] We have the
Misom project meeting this afternoon.

25:48.546 --> 25:50.674
We'll review
the Jeseon-dong coffee shop plans too.

25:50.757 --> 25:53.218
And we need to start preparing
for Greip's flagship store,

25:53.301 --> 25:54.344
so get ready.

25:55.387 --> 25:59.015
Na-yun, is that white mark on his back
a ghost or something?

25:59.099 --> 26:00.892
-It's foundation.
-[Myeong-u] What?

26:00.976 --> 26:02.352
-[door closes]
-Shade 21.

26:03.019 --> 26:03.937
No. Shade 19?

26:04.020 --> 26:07.691
Makeup? Seung-hyo must've had
a passionate morning!

26:07.774 --> 26:10.694
It was intense enough
to leave a mark of a hug on his back!

26:10.777 --> 26:14.739
-Those facial features look familiar.
-[Myeong-u] What?

26:14.823 --> 26:17.951
Who is it? No way. Was it Tae-hui?

26:19.286 --> 26:21.246
Were you two talking about me?

26:21.329 --> 26:22.914
[Myeong-u] Yeah. I mean, no.

26:22.998 --> 26:24.666
-What?
-It's not her.

26:24.749 --> 26:27.252
It's not? Then, who is it?

26:27.335 --> 26:28.962
It's obvious.

26:29.045 --> 26:31.506
-Jeez.
-Who is it?

26:32.340 --> 26:34.259
-What's wrong?
-What? Well…

26:35.302 --> 26:36.386
It's not you.

26:36.469 --> 26:37.470
-Me?
-[Myeong-u] No.

26:37.554 --> 26:39.639
Hey, who is it?

26:39.723 --> 26:41.558
What was that? [chuckles softly]

26:42.642 --> 26:45.270
TEMPERATURE OF TIME - ONGGI KETTLE

26:49.691 --> 26:50.525
What are you doing?

26:50.608 --> 26:52.819
I gave you some Botox
so you'd stop scowling.

26:54.070 --> 26:55.488
I must've been too focused.

26:56.406 --> 26:57.574
You sure that's all?

26:58.450 --> 27:00.160
And not scowling about something else?

27:00.744 --> 27:01.911
Stop trying to find out.

27:04.122 --> 27:05.165
You caught me.

27:06.875 --> 27:09.502
But didn't we agree to make a coffee pot?

27:10.045 --> 27:11.504
It says "kettle" here.

27:11.588 --> 27:15.842
Yeah, I changed it.
I've spoken with the person in charge too.

27:15.925 --> 27:18.178
You didn't even tell me.
But why change it?

27:18.261 --> 27:21.014
There's no romance
if things heat up too quickly.

27:22.349 --> 27:25.643
Turn on the heat
and carefully bring the water to a boil.

27:26.519 --> 27:28.480
I believe in the importance
of taking time.

27:30.065 --> 27:30.899
Like an onggi?

27:32.525 --> 27:33.526
Like love.

27:34.819 --> 27:36.154
[Tae-hui] In my twenties,

27:36.738 --> 27:39.657
I hoped too much
for things to heat up quickly.

27:39.741 --> 27:43.953
But now, I want to focus
on warm and subtle things.

27:44.537 --> 27:45.914
Slowly and for a long time.

27:47.874 --> 27:49.459
You've changed a lot.

27:50.877 --> 27:52.128
It's because of you.

27:53.088 --> 27:55.882
No, it's thanks to you.

27:59.761 --> 28:02.639
Stop being scared.
I won't ask you to take responsibility.

28:04.057 --> 28:06.893
Let's just wait and see.

28:08.019 --> 28:12.148
I'll follow my heart.
You follow yours.

28:14.567 --> 28:16.653
And Seok-ryu will follow hers.

28:17.529 --> 28:19.906
Why would you suddenly bring her up?

28:19.989 --> 28:22.158
It's so easy to get you worked up.

28:23.493 --> 28:26.704
Where did my cool, calm ex-boyfriend go?

28:26.788 --> 28:30.291
You turn into a teenage boy
at the sound of Seok-ryu's name.

28:30.375 --> 28:31.584
It's not that.

28:31.668 --> 28:35.088
-You keep going off-topic, so--
-You're trying way too hard.

28:35.171 --> 28:36.506
This is cute too though.

28:38.758 --> 28:40.093
[exhales]

28:41.761 --> 28:42.762
[smacks lips]

28:43.096 --> 28:44.097
[indistinct chatter]

28:44.180 --> 28:45.348
[amusing music playing]

28:45.432 --> 28:46.725
[Dan-ho] Yeon-du!

28:50.520 --> 28:51.354
Dad.

28:51.438 --> 28:53.481
Did you take the afternoon off again?

28:55.650 --> 28:59.654
Yeah. You had a mild fever this morning.
Let's go home early and rest.

29:00.655 --> 29:02.282
Unbelievable.

29:03.158 --> 29:06.953
What will your company think of me
if you keep acting like this?

29:07.620 --> 29:08.872
What?

29:08.955 --> 29:10.790
They'll think of me as a weak child

29:10.874 --> 29:12.834
who's prone to crying for her dad.

29:13.710 --> 29:17.088
Yeon-du, having days off
is an employee's fundamental right.

29:17.756 --> 29:19.966
Did you forget
I'm a social affairs reporter?

29:20.049 --> 29:21.801
If they treat me unfairly over this,

29:21.885 --> 29:24.137
I don't care who they are.
I'll confront them.

29:25.263 --> 29:26.097
Dad.

29:27.682 --> 29:30.602
Just keep your job until I go to college.

29:33.521 --> 29:34.564
Okay.

29:36.483 --> 29:37.525
Wait for me.

29:38.276 --> 29:40.695
Goodbye. [exclaims]

29:42.238 --> 29:43.323
[sighs]

29:43.406 --> 29:46.451
Why am I the one
who always loses games and pays for lunch?

29:48.328 --> 29:51.414
Hold on. Are they rigging them
behind my back?

29:52.832 --> 29:54.209
That's mine.

29:54.292 --> 29:56.169
-[engine accelerating]
-[horn honking]

29:56.252 --> 29:57.462
[tires screeching]

29:57.545 --> 29:59.255
[horns honking]

30:02.133 --> 30:03.092
[man] Are they drunk?

30:03.176 --> 30:04.385
What?

30:04.469 --> 30:05.720
[dramatic music playing]

30:07.847 --> 30:08.765
Just a moment!

30:11.392 --> 30:12.435
Sir?

30:16.815 --> 30:17.857
Cardiac arrest.

30:17.941 --> 30:20.151
-Someone call 119!
-I'll do it!

30:24.155 --> 30:25.031
[line ringing]

30:25.114 --> 30:27.534
Hello? I'm at the intersection
near Hyereung Kindergarten.

30:27.617 --> 30:29.410
A car just ran into a streetlight.

30:29.494 --> 30:30.870
Do you have a hammer?

30:30.954 --> 30:33.373
Yes, but I think the driver's unconscious.

30:34.290 --> 30:35.416
Yes, I understand.

30:38.086 --> 30:38.962
Please move!

30:47.846 --> 30:48.680
[grunts]

30:50.723 --> 30:51.558
Sir.

30:52.517 --> 30:53.601
Sir?

30:55.854 --> 30:56.771
[seatbelt unlocks]

31:07.907 --> 31:11.578
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, ten,

31:11.661 --> 31:15.373
eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen,
fifteen, sixteen, seventeen, eighteen.

31:15.456 --> 31:16.833
[captivating music playing]

31:31.890 --> 31:33.474
-[man grunting weakly]
-[Mo-eum exhales]

31:33.558 --> 31:36.060
Are you okay? Don't get up.

31:36.144 --> 31:36.978
Stay down.

31:37.061 --> 31:39.564
I know it's uncomfortable,
but let's turn to your side.

31:39.981 --> 31:40.815
Okay.

31:43.693 --> 31:44.819
It'll be okay.

31:46.905 --> 31:48.323
[Mo-eum breathing heavily]

31:55.330 --> 31:57.457
[breathing heavily]

32:01.586 --> 32:02.587
[exhales]

32:02.670 --> 32:04.255
[amusing music playing]

32:08.343 --> 32:09.260
[exhales]

32:11.512 --> 32:14.265
Jae-suk! What are you looking for?

32:14.349 --> 32:15.600
-My sunglasses.
-[In-suk] What?

32:15.683 --> 32:17.936
I had them on just a second ago.

32:18.019 --> 32:20.605
-Goodness. Hands on your head.
-[In-suk laughing]

32:22.023 --> 32:24.233
-My goodness. I don't believe it.
-[laughing]

32:25.068 --> 32:29.155
Hey, it wasn't right under my nose.
It was right on my head!

32:29.238 --> 32:32.700
Jeez, is it my age?
Why am I so forgetful these days?

32:32.784 --> 32:34.035
Don't get me started.

32:34.118 --> 32:36.579
I needed to go to the post office
to send a package yesterday.

32:36.663 --> 32:38.873
I put my shoes on and left
but forgot the box.

32:38.957 --> 32:42.835
-Goodness. That's so sad.
-What's wrong with you?

32:42.919 --> 32:44.796
I can't trust myself anymore.

32:44.879 --> 32:47.173
I can't even remember words when talking.

32:47.256 --> 32:49.342
I called the washer a vacuum
and the vacuum a fridge.

32:49.425 --> 32:50.843
And I call Dong-jin Seok-ryu.

32:50.927 --> 32:54.639
Hey, this gastrodia root extract
is supposed to be a gift from the heavens.

32:54.722 --> 32:56.975
They say it contains neurotransmitters,

32:57.058 --> 32:59.477
so it improves blood flow
and helps prevent dementia.

32:59.560 --> 33:01.145
-Really?
-Try it.

33:01.229 --> 33:02.730
-Give me one.
-Another extract?

33:02.814 --> 33:04.941
Don't rely on these things.
Open it for me.

33:05.024 --> 33:06.192
-Open it for you? Okay.
-Yeah.

33:06.275 --> 33:09.404
Get in the habit of writing notes
if you're worried about dementia.

33:09.487 --> 33:12.407
-[In-suk] Notes? Okay. Here.
-[Hye-suk] Read books and newspapers too.

33:12.490 --> 33:14.242
You still haven't fixed that habit?

33:14.325 --> 33:15.243
-[Hye-suk] What?
-What?

33:15.326 --> 33:17.745
You can't go a day without showing off.
That bad habit.

33:17.829 --> 33:19.288
-Hey.
-[In-suk] What's with you?

33:19.372 --> 33:23.251
You two are the closest
but are so harsh when you argue.

33:23.334 --> 33:25.169
Yeah, Mi-suk.

33:25.253 --> 33:28.006
You're irritated
because Seok-ryu's fiancé's here.

33:28.089 --> 33:30.258
Don't be sensitive
and take it out on us…

33:32.010 --> 33:33.469
Where did you hear that?

33:33.553 --> 33:36.014
-Dong-jin. I went to the gym this morning.
-[In-suk gasps]

33:36.097 --> 33:38.224
I'm going to kill that punk!

33:38.307 --> 33:39.392
Damn it.

33:39.475 --> 33:41.436
-[Jae-suk] Hey!
-Can't keep a secret in this town.

33:41.519 --> 33:44.397
I heard he was begging to get her back!

33:44.480 --> 33:45.565
And why wouldn't he?

33:45.648 --> 33:47.442
-She's so beautiful!
-That's right.

33:47.525 --> 33:50.445
Seok-ryu looks just like you
when you were young!

33:50.528 --> 33:51.863
She does take after me.

33:51.946 --> 33:54.449
Yeah, Mi-suk was so popular
in high school.

33:54.532 --> 33:56.743
-[Jae-suk] That's right.
-You remember too, right?

33:56.826 --> 33:58.536
I don't know. I don't remember.

33:58.619 --> 34:00.038
What?

34:00.121 --> 34:02.206
Right. That's how you were back then.

34:02.290 --> 34:04.625
-[Jae-suk] Yeah.
-Mi-suk was so pretty.

34:04.709 --> 34:05.543
-Hey.
-So pretty.

34:05.626 --> 34:09.088
[Jae-suk] She's popular like her mom.
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree.

34:09.172 --> 34:12.467
Don't take him back
no matter how much he begs!

34:12.550 --> 34:15.178
-He's a despicable bastard!
-[In-suk] Right.

34:15.261 --> 34:17.388
He's not that bad.

34:17.472 --> 34:20.433
Yes, he is! He disgraced her
with a canceled engagement!

34:20.516 --> 34:21.350
That's right!

34:21.434 --> 34:23.895
Crushing him into a pulp
wouldn't be enough punishment.

34:23.978 --> 34:26.314
Hey, what do you mean,
"crush him into a pulp"?

34:26.814 --> 34:29.067
My son-in-law's not some herb extract!

34:29.150 --> 34:30.985
You're all so crude!

34:31.652 --> 34:33.237
-Forget this!
-[Jae-suk] Hey!

34:33.321 --> 34:35.823
-That's not what I meant, Mi-suk.
-[Hye-suk] My gosh.

34:35.907 --> 34:38.409
-What on earth were we supposed to say?
-[Jae-suk] I swear.

34:38.493 --> 34:39.660
She's in menopause.

34:39.744 --> 34:41.621
-Mood swings.
-[Hye-suk] We all are.

34:41.704 --> 34:44.874
-[Jae-suk] This is so hard.
-Pomegranate juice is good for that.

34:44.957 --> 34:47.919
-Open that for me.
-Wait just a second. Mi-suk!

34:48.711 --> 34:50.421
She's not going to get over it.

34:50.505 --> 34:52.882
-Stop drinking that.
-Just leave her.

34:57.136 --> 34:58.221
[Hyeon-jun] Seok-ryu.

35:01.474 --> 35:02.391
Wait…

35:05.061 --> 35:06.229
[exclaiming in pain]

35:07.063 --> 35:10.149
Hyeon-jun, what's wrong?
Are you okay? Did you hurt yourself?

35:10.233 --> 35:11.901
-[whinces]
-[Seok-ryu] Are you okay?

35:12.485 --> 35:13.945
I got you.

35:15.446 --> 35:18.866
-My acting's improved a lot, hasn't it?
-What on earth are you doing?

35:19.784 --> 35:20.785
I'm sorry.

35:21.369 --> 35:23.496
You wouldn't have turned around otherwise.

35:24.789 --> 35:26.833
Seok-ryu,

35:27.416 --> 35:29.001
I messed up back then.

35:29.085 --> 35:31.838
I know I wasn't good enough.

35:32.839 --> 35:34.882
I should've tried harder
to be more understanding.

35:34.966 --> 35:36.884
No, you didn't do anything wrong.

35:38.094 --> 35:39.887
I know you did your best.

35:41.139 --> 35:44.767
I was too overwhelmed.
I only thought about myself.

35:44.851 --> 35:46.519
You had no other choice--

35:46.602 --> 35:47.562
I'll get going.

35:48.771 --> 35:50.148
Let's get something to eat.

35:50.690 --> 35:53.526
If it's for the last time,
I'm fine with that. Just once.

35:54.485 --> 35:55.862
Let's grab a meal together.

36:03.953 --> 36:04.787
Dan-ho?

36:05.371 --> 36:06.497
Yeon-du!

36:09.250 --> 36:11.252
She said she had something to give you.

36:11.335 --> 36:12.628
-What?
-[Dan-ho] Go ahead.

36:15.298 --> 36:17.175
Stoop down a little.

36:17.758 --> 36:18.634
Like this?

36:23.931 --> 36:25.391
[chuckles softly]

36:28.227 --> 36:30.354
-[pleasant music playing]
-[exclaims]

36:37.028 --> 36:37.862
Does it sting?

36:37.945 --> 36:41.741
No, it doesn't sting at all.
It feels so warm.

36:41.824 --> 36:45.286
It shouldn't feel warm.
That means bacteria got in it.

36:45.995 --> 36:47.455
-Just a second.
-[Mo-eum] Okay.

37:00.176 --> 37:01.010
[Yeon-du] There.

37:01.093 --> 37:02.803
Wow, Yeon-du.

37:02.887 --> 37:05.640
I'll get better in no time
because of your ointment.

37:05.723 --> 37:06.891
Thank you.

37:08.517 --> 37:10.102
-You know what?
-What?

37:10.186 --> 37:12.647
You were so cool today!

37:12.730 --> 37:15.608
Even though you didn't have webs
coming out of your hands,

37:15.691 --> 37:18.194
you were way cooler than Spider-Man.

37:18.277 --> 37:19.946
[Mo-eum] Really?

37:20.029 --> 37:22.698
Hearing that gives me so much strength.
Thank you.

37:23.741 --> 37:26.452
Come with us if you're getting off work.
We'll give you a ride.

37:27.036 --> 37:28.788
What do you think? Should I come?

37:28.871 --> 37:29.789
Let's go.

37:29.872 --> 37:30.998
[chuckles]

37:46.722 --> 37:47.932
Are you feeling hot?

37:48.015 --> 37:50.893
Yeon-du has a cold,
so I can't turn on the AC right now.

37:50.977 --> 37:52.311
Yeah, I'm fine.

37:52.395 --> 37:54.272
But it looks like you're hot.

37:54.355 --> 37:55.773
A little bit.

37:56.524 --> 38:00.945
-Do you mind if I take off my jacket?
-Sure, you don't have to ask.

38:11.664 --> 38:13.833
-[exhales]
-[engine accelerating]

38:17.461 --> 38:20.589
I think Yeon-du has completely fallen
for you today.

38:22.008 --> 38:25.469
At last! I finally did it.

38:26.053 --> 38:27.722
I'm not taking this off tonight.

38:28.514 --> 38:30.516
Do you get hurt often like that?

38:31.225 --> 38:33.728
It's not often. Just sometimes.

38:34.270 --> 38:36.063
Because all sorts of incidents happen.

38:37.189 --> 38:38.649
Don't you get scared?

38:38.733 --> 38:40.276
Like what happened earlier?

38:41.110 --> 38:43.821
No way. None of that scares me.

38:44.447 --> 38:45.823
Other things scare me.

38:47.658 --> 38:50.244
"What if I can't save the patient?"

38:51.412 --> 38:54.915
"What if I'm too late
and can't do anything?"

38:55.624 --> 38:59.628
You're so brave. I admire you.

39:01.422 --> 39:04.675
You're glorifying me
because of what I said.

39:04.759 --> 39:05.760
It's true though.

39:06.260 --> 39:09.930
When I saw you, I realized
we don't have to look far for heroes.

39:10.014 --> 39:11.599
They're close to us.

39:11.682 --> 39:14.226
I was just doing my job.

39:15.936 --> 39:17.063
Oh.

39:17.188 --> 39:19.315
But I did meet a real hero once.

39:20.066 --> 39:21.067
-Really?
-Yes.

39:21.150 --> 39:22.777
-Who was it?
-Well…

39:23.402 --> 39:26.405
Once, we were rushing
a child to the hospital.

39:26.489 --> 39:28.824
-Right.
-At that time, the roads were blocked.

39:28.908 --> 39:31.077
We couldn't move forward at all.

39:32.119 --> 39:35.623
That's when someone got out of his car,

39:36.165 --> 39:38.584
and he directed traffic to clear the road.

39:39.335 --> 39:41.295
There was like a superhero.

39:42.588 --> 39:45.049
It felt like I had met
the man of my dreams.

39:45.758 --> 39:48.260
I don't know who he is,
but I call him Mudflat Man.

39:48.844 --> 39:50.096
Mudflat Man?

39:50.179 --> 39:53.182
Yes, he had the funniest T-shirt on.

39:53.766 --> 39:55.810
It said, "I love you, mudflats."

39:55.893 --> 39:57.061
[tires screech]

39:57.144 --> 39:59.105
-[Mo-eum grunts]
-[amusing music playing]

40:00.815 --> 40:01.899
Are you okay?

40:01.982 --> 40:04.819
-[Dan-ho] I'm sorry.
-Did the lights…

40:04.902 --> 40:06.445
I LOVE YOU, MUDFLATS

40:06.529 --> 40:08.656
I LOVE YOU, MUDFLATS

40:11.534 --> 40:12.785
[Dan-ho groans]

40:12.868 --> 40:15.788
Dan-ho, where did you get this shirt?

40:16.455 --> 40:20.793
Well, the thing is…
while I was covering a story,

40:20.876 --> 40:24.255
I met an environmental group called
the Mudflat Guardians who gave one to me.

40:24.338 --> 40:25.548
Mudflat Guardians?

40:25.631 --> 40:27.216
[Dan-ho] Yes.

40:27.299 --> 40:28.634
Holy cow.

40:30.469 --> 40:31.846
So you might know him then.

40:32.638 --> 40:34.557
Who else is in that group?

40:34.640 --> 40:37.518
I don't know.
They're mostly older men and women.

40:37.601 --> 40:39.270
[Mo-eum] Not them. I mean, young guys.

40:39.353 --> 40:44.191
So I didn't see his face,
but he seemed to be about our age.

40:44.900 --> 40:47.486
I think he was as tall…

40:48.821 --> 40:49.780
as you…

40:53.826 --> 40:55.828
[horn honking]

41:00.458 --> 41:01.333
[exhales]

41:03.085 --> 41:04.420
Good night!

41:04.503 --> 41:05.421
[Dan-ho] Wait…

41:05.504 --> 41:07.173
What? Why are you following me?

41:08.048 --> 41:10.468
Well, I had something to give you.

41:11.051 --> 41:12.219
Just a moment.

41:13.429 --> 41:14.513
So…

41:18.017 --> 41:19.393
[groans softly]

41:19.477 --> 41:20.603
[Mo-eum] Seriously?

41:22.396 --> 41:25.107
Why do you have
so many medical supplies in your bag?

41:25.191 --> 41:26.984
They're all for you.

41:28.068 --> 41:29.111
The pharmacy said

41:29.195 --> 41:31.822
you need different medications
for each healing stage.

41:33.157 --> 41:35.367
This one prevents infection.

41:35.451 --> 41:38.037
This prevents scabs from forming.

41:38.662 --> 41:40.623
This one's for scars.

41:47.755 --> 41:49.548
Please don't get hurt again.

41:53.886 --> 41:55.721
I have to go park my car.

42:02.269 --> 42:03.270
[breath trembles]

42:03.729 --> 42:05.439
[Mo-eum breathing heavily]

42:09.693 --> 42:10.986
[panting]

42:11.070 --> 42:13.239
Mudflat Man was the reporter.

42:13.322 --> 42:15.866
-[exhales]
-[heart thumping]

42:17.284 --> 42:18.118
What?

42:19.286 --> 42:22.206
Why is my heart pounding?

42:22.957 --> 42:25.042
What is it, a drum or something?
[exclaims]

42:29.547 --> 42:30.756
[dramatic whoosh]

42:32.675 --> 42:34.802
PERFECT MATCH

42:34.885 --> 42:36.053
I knew it.

42:36.136 --> 42:38.597
Those pale, squashed facial features.

42:39.139 --> 42:40.432
I'm sure it's Seok-ryu.

42:41.058 --> 42:42.935
I knew this would happen!

42:43.018 --> 42:45.980
I was worried about her from the start.
Damn it!

42:46.063 --> 42:47.606
[machine beeping]

42:48.774 --> 42:51.151
-[machine beeping]
-[Na-yun exclaiming]

42:51.235 --> 42:53.404
[amusing music playing]

42:53.487 --> 42:55.197
-What are you doing?
-Miss.

42:55.281 --> 42:57.741
You are not a cheetah.

42:57.825 --> 43:00.077
Of course, you're not a puma
or a jaguar either.

43:00.160 --> 43:01.912
What are you talking about?

43:01.996 --> 43:04.748
You should run at a speed
that's appropriate for humans.

43:04.832 --> 43:07.167
I didn't sign up for a personal trainer.

43:07.251 --> 43:10.087
I'm in the middle of my own workout,
so can you go away?

43:10.588 --> 43:12.131
You're making me uncomfortable.

43:12.631 --> 43:15.342
[machine beeping]

43:16.343 --> 43:18.095
[machine beeping]

43:18.178 --> 43:20.806
You'll break the equipment
and yourself at this rate.

43:20.889 --> 43:23.809
-Don't worry about it. Leave me alone.
-[machine beeping]

43:24.518 --> 43:26.270
[machine beeping]

43:26.353 --> 43:27.688
[Na-yun] Hey, come on.

43:27.771 --> 43:29.189
What do I do?

43:29.273 --> 43:30.482
I can't allow that.

43:30.566 --> 43:32.276
What on earth are you doing?

43:32.359 --> 43:33.611
-[machine beeping]
-[groans]

43:33.694 --> 43:34.903
This is perfect for you.

43:34.987 --> 43:38.490
You can run straight
to the Serengeti at this speed.

43:38.574 --> 43:40.993
-What's wrong with you?
-Eyes on the road!

43:41.076 --> 43:42.369
Okay, go.

43:42.453 --> 43:44.079
[both breathing heavily]

43:44.830 --> 43:46.165
[Dong-jin] Look, zebras!

43:46.248 --> 43:47.833
[indistinct chatter on TV]

43:52.254 --> 43:53.380
I'm watching my show.

43:53.464 --> 43:55.382
Why do you have to stand
in front of the TV?

43:55.466 --> 43:57.092
Today wasn't a coincidence, was it?

43:57.176 --> 43:58.302
[groans softly]

43:58.385 --> 44:02.056
Hyeon-jun came here,
and you suddenly had me dress up.

44:02.139 --> 44:05.017
Gosh, I applied lotion,
but why are my heels so cracked?

44:05.100 --> 44:07.269
Look at this. You're changing the subject.

44:08.187 --> 44:10.439
I can clearly see
what you're trying to do.

44:10.522 --> 44:13.651
Don't do this anymore.
It won't change anything.

44:13.734 --> 44:15.736
This won't do.
Let's go to the sauna tomorrow.

44:16.779 --> 44:18.989
-No, I'm not going.
-Why not? It's nice.

44:19.073 --> 44:21.283
We can soak in hot water and exfoliate.

44:21.367 --> 44:23.869
Right.
Hasn't it been years since you exfoliated?

44:23.952 --> 44:27.998
-Gross. I can't associate with you.
-Body scrubs can handle that, okay?

44:28.082 --> 44:30.417
What's so great
about scrubbing your flesh off?

44:30.501 --> 44:33.337
Above all,
I hate getting in the water with others.

44:33.420 --> 44:34.672
-Why?
-It's uncomfortable.

44:34.755 --> 44:37.049
Why would you sit around naked
with other strangers?

44:37.132 --> 44:39.093
Who cares? We're all women.

44:39.176 --> 44:41.345
Also, you're my daughter.

44:41.428 --> 44:43.472
Isn't it nice to go with your mother?

44:43.555 --> 44:44.973
Maybe when I was younger,

44:45.057 --> 44:47.768
but we're independent
and separate entities now.

44:47.851 --> 44:50.729
You still have that kind
of outdated fantasy?

44:50.813 --> 44:53.023
Yeah, I'm old-fashioned and from the '80s.

44:53.107 --> 44:55.401
You're modern and sophisticated.
Good for you, you brat.

44:55.484 --> 44:57.236
How sophisticated of you.

44:57.319 --> 44:58.529
Must be nice.

44:59.113 --> 45:01.865
-[door opens, closes]
-[scoffs] Jeez.

45:02.366 --> 45:04.701
-[door closes]
-[dog barks distantly]

45:13.001 --> 45:16.630
-Why are you walking around late at night?
-Is that a dog I hear barking?

45:17.714 --> 45:20.300
Don't you watch the news?
The world's a scary place.

45:21.051 --> 45:23.387
Did someone turn on the local station?

45:23.470 --> 45:25.973
It's making
the whole neighborhood noisy. Jeez.

45:26.056 --> 45:28.225
Forget it. Fine, do whatever you want.

45:33.439 --> 45:35.023
[cats meowing in the distance]

45:42.197 --> 45:43.657
[suspenseful music playing]

45:43.740 --> 45:45.159
[footsteps approaching]

45:52.291 --> 45:53.876
[suspenseful music building up]

46:06.638 --> 46:07.848
[suspenseful music fades]

46:07.931 --> 46:09.725
You crazy bastard! You scared me!

46:10.642 --> 46:13.896
-Quiet! This is a residential area.
-That's not what's important!

46:13.979 --> 46:16.648
Why the hell did you follow me
and scare me like that?

46:16.732 --> 46:18.567
Why did you suddenly run like that?

46:18.650 --> 46:20.861
Because I thought someone was chasing me.

46:20.944 --> 46:22.529
You could've called my name.

46:22.613 --> 46:25.574
Well, you could've looked back.
Why were you only looking straight?

46:25.657 --> 46:27.993
You should've called out and reassured me.

46:28.076 --> 46:30.370
You should've checked first
before blindly running.

46:31.997 --> 46:33.081
[exhales]

46:35.083 --> 46:36.335
Jeez.

46:39.129 --> 46:40.714
I think this is our problem.

46:41.590 --> 46:45.427
We pass things off on each other,
make excuses, and shift the blame.

46:47.387 --> 46:48.722
We don't say what we need to say,

46:48.805 --> 46:51.308
so we go around in circles
and end up fighting,

46:52.184 --> 46:53.519
like last time.

46:54.686 --> 46:56.063
[breathing heavily]

46:56.146 --> 46:57.689
What I wanted to say…

46:58.857 --> 47:00.025
wasn't that.

47:02.361 --> 47:03.529
I wanted to answer you.

47:06.406 --> 47:07.824
That day,

47:09.451 --> 47:11.411
you asked me what I meant.

47:12.037 --> 47:14.289
Stop driving me crazy!

47:14.373 --> 47:17.417
Back then and now, you keep doing this…

47:17.501 --> 47:18.710
so I feel like…

47:20.837 --> 47:22.923
I'm going to lose my mind because of you!

47:27.553 --> 47:29.680
-What I meant was…
-Don't.

47:31.306 --> 47:32.516
Look,

47:32.599 --> 47:34.309
right now… [exhales]

47:35.227 --> 47:37.896
…I have a bunch of error messages
popped up in my head.

47:38.814 --> 47:43.318
It's overloaded and has stopped working,
so I can't perform any new tasks.

47:44.069 --> 47:45.529
So, later.

47:46.488 --> 47:47.322
Tell me later.

47:51.285 --> 47:53.161
-Later when?
-Just later.

47:53.745 --> 47:57.374
Things are pretty complicated
for me right now.

47:59.918 --> 48:01.336
Because of Hyeon-jun?

48:02.004 --> 48:03.922
No, it's not because of that.

48:05.007 --> 48:07.384
There's just a lot of other things.

48:08.594 --> 48:09.511
[smacks lips]

48:09.845 --> 48:10.846
[inhales]

48:13.849 --> 48:14.683
Yeah, okay.

48:16.351 --> 48:18.478
I'll hold off on answering you.

48:18.562 --> 48:21.690
I'll postpone it
until your error messages are gone.

48:23.525 --> 48:26.695
I'll wait until things
aren't complicated for you anymore.

48:27.529 --> 48:29.531
-Seung-hyo, I--
-[Seung-hyo] Later.

48:30.991 --> 48:32.659
You say it later too.

48:38.915 --> 48:40.167
But let me ask you one thing.

48:42.377 --> 48:44.421
Are you going to keep seeing that jerk?

48:45.088 --> 48:48.425
No, I don't plan on it.

48:49.968 --> 48:51.053
You mean it?

48:55.057 --> 48:56.391
All right, then.

48:57.976 --> 49:00.062
[mellow music playing]

49:01.063 --> 49:03.690
I think we've done plenty
of walking and running now.

49:04.775 --> 49:05.609
Let's go home.

49:06.318 --> 49:07.319
Okay.

49:09.112 --> 49:10.113
[clears throat]

49:18.830 --> 49:19.831
[Seung-hyo] Go on ahead.

49:20.874 --> 49:22.876
I'll definitely be behind you this time,

49:23.752 --> 49:25.379
so you don't have to look back.

49:28.298 --> 49:29.383
Don't be scared.

49:52.531 --> 49:53.865
[music continues playing]

50:21.393 --> 50:22.769
[Hye-suk inhales]

50:28.900 --> 50:29.901
[groans softly]

50:42.873 --> 50:43.707
Mmm.

50:52.507 --> 50:53.508
[phone chimes]

50:53.592 --> 50:55.719
MY BIRTHDAY
TODAY

50:55.802 --> 50:57.220
[amusing music playing]

51:07.606 --> 51:09.232
-Where are you going?
-It's an emergency.

51:09.316 --> 51:10.942
There was a 17-car pileup this morning.

51:11.026 --> 51:12.319
Is that so?

51:12.402 --> 51:13.820
Then, when do you get home--

51:17.699 --> 51:18.700
[door closes]

51:21.036 --> 51:21.953
[knock on door]

51:22.037 --> 51:23.121
Seung-hyo?

51:36.384 --> 51:37.969
He must've left early.

51:59.074 --> 52:01.076
I'll be there soon. I'm almost there.

52:14.506 --> 52:15.465
What's wrong?

52:15.549 --> 52:17.634
Why did you call me at dawn…

52:25.976 --> 52:28.603
[Tae-hui] I wanted you
to be the first to see it.

52:28.687 --> 52:29.855
It's our first sample.

52:30.856 --> 52:33.358
You told me to come
for something big. This was it?

52:33.441 --> 52:36.778
This is something big.
It came out beautifully.

52:37.487 --> 52:39.322
It does look nice.

52:39.406 --> 52:41.658
The body is round like an onggi.

52:41.741 --> 52:44.077
The spout is like the eaves
of a traditional roof.

52:44.160 --> 52:46.705
You wanted to preserve
the subtle curves of Korean design.

52:47.330 --> 52:50.083
Isn't it nice?
Isn't it similar to your sketches?

52:50.709 --> 52:52.168
I told you it was nice.

52:52.252 --> 52:54.170
Are you longing for praise these days?

52:54.254 --> 52:55.255
No.

52:55.755 --> 52:59.467
I only long for praise from you.
I'm starved for it.

52:59.551 --> 53:01.136
Let's keep things professional.

53:01.636 --> 53:03.680
Do you usually get a lot
of broken jars like that?

53:04.639 --> 53:06.016
[Tae-hui] Oh, those?

53:06.099 --> 53:07.392
Of course.

53:07.976 --> 53:10.312
-And it's not due to a lack of skill?
-[Tae-hui scoffs]

53:12.606 --> 53:14.858
Look here, Mr. Architect.

53:15.650 --> 53:19.195
Do things always go according to plan
on site just because you design them?

53:19.279 --> 53:20.947
A wise answer to a dumb question.

53:21.031 --> 53:23.825
No matter how carefully I shape the clay,

53:23.909 --> 53:26.578
no one knows
how it'll come out from the fire.

53:27.662 --> 53:30.874
Will it become a perfectly formed vessel?

53:30.957 --> 53:34.461
Or will it crack and shatter to pieces?

53:34.544 --> 53:36.755
You won't know
until it goes into the kiln.

53:36.838 --> 53:38.256
[mellow music playing]

53:41.217 --> 53:43.470
That sounded
like such a great quote. Right?

53:45.221 --> 53:49.851
Not only am I beautiful
and make onggi well but I'm also eloquent.

53:49.935 --> 53:53.688
You're so great at praising yourself
that you don't need my help.

53:53.772 --> 53:55.398
I said I'm still starved for it.

53:56.858 --> 53:59.486
Let's get something good to eat in Seoul.

54:00.737 --> 54:02.113
I'll go and change.

54:19.381 --> 54:21.299
-[Hye-suk] Hello.
-Hello, Ambassador.

54:21.383 --> 54:23.802
Is the vice minister inside?
We're having lunch.

54:23.885 --> 54:28.348
I'm sorry, but the minister
called for him today, so he's gone.

54:29.474 --> 54:32.811
Goodness. He did tell me to let you know.

54:32.894 --> 54:36.147
It's going to take a while,
so he asked for a rain check on lunch.

54:36.231 --> 54:38.733
Is that so? Okay.

54:38.817 --> 54:39.776
Have a nice day, ma'am.

54:39.859 --> 54:41.111
-You too.
-Thank you.

54:54.791 --> 54:56.960
[Hye-suk] What are you all doing tonight?

54:57.043 --> 54:58.920
LAVENDER

55:03.758 --> 55:04.759
[exclaims]

55:09.472 --> 55:11.349
Please don't get hurt again.

55:11.433 --> 55:13.685
[heart thumping]

55:13.768 --> 55:14.769
What's going on?

55:15.437 --> 55:19.733
Why is my heart thumping?
Are you kidding me?

55:20.525 --> 55:21.860
Why is it beating faster?

55:22.736 --> 55:24.571
Why did it skip a beat this time?

55:25.655 --> 55:27.657
[Min-ho] Why are you
grumbling to yourself?

55:27.741 --> 55:30.744
-I thought you were with someone.
-No, it's nothing.

55:31.411 --> 55:34.330
[Jeong-u] Ms. Jung,
why is your face so red?

55:34.414 --> 55:36.291
-It's red?
-[Jeong-u] Yeah.

55:36.916 --> 55:38.668
-[Min-ho] Do you have a fever?
-No.

55:38.752 --> 55:41.129
Are you sure your cut isn't infected?

55:41.212 --> 55:43.089
No, it's not that.

55:43.173 --> 55:45.633
I've applied an excessive amount
of ointment.

55:45.717 --> 55:47.052
Okay, let's go.

55:48.762 --> 55:49.637
Let's go.

55:49.721 --> 55:51.514
[pop song playing in the background]

55:53.641 --> 55:55.560
CONDITIONS IN THE FIELD FOR PARAMEDICS

55:55.643 --> 55:56.853
ASSAULTS ON EMTS RISE

56:06.488 --> 56:08.740
What are you looking at so seriously?

56:09.699 --> 56:14.412
Yeong-in, did you know
almost 14% of firefighters suffer

56:14.496 --> 56:18.666
from PTSD, depression,
and sleep disorders?

56:18.750 --> 56:20.210
I'm sure they do.

56:21.127 --> 56:25.340
Their job exposes them to a higher risk
of danger than the general public.

56:25.423 --> 56:28.885
There are about 300 cases of assault
on paramedics each year.

56:28.968 --> 56:31.721
Most offenders avoid punishment
because they were drunk.

56:32.847 --> 56:37.352
Dan-ho, you've suddenly become
very interested in firefighters.

56:37.435 --> 56:38.311
Oh.

56:38.812 --> 56:40.688
There's a paramedic I know.

56:41.481 --> 56:43.650
I've seen her be treated badly before.

56:43.733 --> 56:46.569
I've also seen her risk her life
to rescue others too.

56:48.196 --> 56:49.739
So you're going to write an article?

56:50.323 --> 56:51.407
What?

56:51.491 --> 56:53.368
Give it your best, okay?

56:53.868 --> 56:54.869
Good luck!

56:55.578 --> 56:57.872
We might cover a story,

56:57.956 --> 57:01.751
but we can't truly understand it
without firsthand experience.

57:03.294 --> 57:07.590
It really becomes your story
after you go through it yourself.

57:08.800 --> 57:11.594
I didn't know being a working mom
would be this hard.

57:11.678 --> 57:15.723
-I got a call from the school today.
-Yeong-in, I just thought of a new story!

57:15.807 --> 57:18.101
Can you excuse me… I mean, I have to go.

57:21.438 --> 57:22.272
[chuckles softly]

57:22.897 --> 57:26.067
I don't know what it is,
but the spark in his eyes is back.

57:28.570 --> 57:32.073
[Tae-hui] This place is really good.
The food's clean and the view's nice.

57:33.658 --> 57:34.784
Oh?

57:37.704 --> 57:38.705
[groans softly]

57:39.539 --> 57:41.416
-Hello.
-Hello.

57:44.294 --> 57:47.505
Seok-ryu, we came to eat too.
Fancy running into you here.

57:48.173 --> 57:49.299
I know.

57:49.382 --> 57:50.758
[Tae-hui] It's nice to see you.

57:51.885 --> 57:54.053
But since we each have company,

57:54.137 --> 57:56.598
I think it'll be uncomfortable
for us to sit here.

57:56.681 --> 57:58.224
Would you like a new table?

57:58.308 --> 58:00.435
-Yes.
-No, it's fine. We'll sit over there.

58:00.518 --> 58:03.188
-Let's just sit.
-Yeah, sure.

58:18.077 --> 58:18.912
[inhales]

58:20.580 --> 58:21.706
[mellow music playing]

58:27.253 --> 58:30.048
How is it? Is the food okay?

58:30.131 --> 58:31.758
Yeah, it's fine.

58:31.841 --> 58:35.845
I'm glad. I put some effort into this.
It's been a while since our last date.

58:36.804 --> 58:38.723
I've been curious about something.

58:40.266 --> 58:41.100
What is that?

58:42.060 --> 58:43.978
It's the japchae I made.

58:44.812 --> 58:46.481
I've been taking cooking classes.

58:46.564 --> 58:50.026
When it comes to cooking,
you're good enough to start an academy.

58:50.109 --> 58:52.362
I'm studying
for a Korean Food Craftsman certification.

58:53.154 --> 58:55.573
I want to do it professionally.

58:55.657 --> 58:57.784
Really? That's great.

58:59.077 --> 59:00.787
But are cooking classes enough?

59:01.829 --> 59:03.540
How about going to cooking school?

59:04.290 --> 59:08.002
The CIA is nice.
They have a campus in California.

59:08.086 --> 59:09.254
[Seok-ryu] I don't know.

59:09.337 --> 59:11.631
Tuition wouldn't be cheap.

59:11.714 --> 59:13.591
I haven't thought that far ahead yet.

59:14.259 --> 59:15.802
[Hyeon-jun] You can take your time.

59:16.261 --> 59:20.181
But can I try your japchae?

59:20.932 --> 59:24.686
[Seok-ryu] What? I don't think you can eat
food from the outside here.

59:25.520 --> 59:26.688
Excuse me?

59:28.147 --> 59:30.608
I have a favor to ask.

59:33.111 --> 59:38.366
Someone very special to me made this food.

59:38.449 --> 59:42.662
I know it might be against the rules,
but can I open it and just try a little?

59:43.788 --> 59:47.125
We normally don't allow that,
so please make it quick.

59:47.208 --> 59:48.334
Thank you.

59:48.835 --> 59:51.754
Your boyfriend is very romantic.

59:58.136 --> 59:59.345
[exhales]

01:00:04.976 --> 01:00:05.977
[slurps]

01:00:07.645 --> 01:00:08.479
[exclaims]

01:00:09.981 --> 01:00:11.232
This is so good.

01:00:12.984 --> 01:00:15.111
This is the best japchae I've ever tasted.

01:00:17.822 --> 01:00:18.698
[exclaims]

01:00:22.619 --> 01:00:24.203
Want me to get you a new knife?

01:00:24.287 --> 01:00:26.706
No. [clears throat]
The steak's a little tough.

01:00:28.791 --> 01:00:31.794
Fresco wants to see us next week.
Do you have time?

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:35.256
-Even if I didn't, I'll make time.
-Right.

01:00:35.757 --> 01:00:38.217
Remember Hye-won
from when we signed the contract?

01:00:38.885 --> 01:00:40.928
She asked about our relationship.

01:00:41.012 --> 01:00:45.141
So I said you were my ex-boyfriend,
but we still like each other.

01:00:47.352 --> 01:00:49.062
Why would you make things up like that?

01:00:49.562 --> 01:00:52.357
She looked interested in you,
so I made a preemptive move.

01:00:52.440 --> 01:00:54.651
Correct that before the next meeting.

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:57.612
And don't lie like that ever again.

01:00:58.780 --> 01:01:01.783
Liars are who I hate
the most in this world.

01:01:02.533 --> 01:01:04.952
Not keeping a promise
is a type of lie too.

01:01:05.036 --> 01:01:05.870
What?

01:01:05.953 --> 01:01:08.706
Like secretly meeting someone
they said they wouldn't.

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:09.999
[coughing]

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:11.751
[amusing music playing]

01:01:13.670 --> 01:01:14.504
Are you okay?

01:01:14.587 --> 01:01:16.756
-[Seok-ryu coughing]
-[Hyeon-jun] Drink some water.

01:01:20.718 --> 01:01:23.471
You should chew your food thoroughly.

01:01:25.056 --> 01:01:26.808
I'm fine.
It just went down the wrong pipe.

01:01:27.392 --> 01:01:29.310
People might think it's a big deal.

01:01:32.855 --> 01:01:35.108
-[clears throat]
-[Hyeon-jun] It's a big deal to me.

01:01:35.191 --> 01:01:37.068
Even the smallest things bother me.

01:01:37.151 --> 01:01:38.528
And I want to take care of you.

01:01:40.113 --> 01:01:43.199
It's just like before,
and it still hasn't changed.

01:01:44.450 --> 01:01:46.536
I have to go to the restroom.

01:01:47.704 --> 01:01:48.663
[Hyeon-jun] Okay.

01:01:58.214 --> 01:01:59.841
Didn't you say you wouldn't see him?

01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:01.759
What's it to you?

01:02:01.843 --> 01:02:05.012
-And you're one to talk.
-Are you talking about Tae-hui?

01:02:05.972 --> 01:02:08.474
-You know we're doing a project together.
-Right.

01:02:08.558 --> 01:02:10.768
You came to eat at a hotel for work.

01:02:10.852 --> 01:02:11.978
You're a great businessman.

01:02:12.061 --> 01:02:14.647
And you? You're eating with someone
you have no business with.

01:02:15.690 --> 01:02:17.275
[Tae-hui] There you are, Seok-ryu.

01:02:17.358 --> 01:02:18.568
I wanted to say bye.

01:02:19.402 --> 01:02:20.236
[Seok-ryu] To me?

01:02:20.778 --> 01:02:22.822
[Tae-hui] I got some wine
to go while paying.

01:02:22.905 --> 01:02:24.031
This is yours.

01:02:24.115 --> 01:02:26.367
No, thank you. I don't drink wine.

01:02:26.451 --> 01:02:28.119
It's fine.

01:02:28.202 --> 01:02:30.079
Then, give it to your boyfriend.

01:02:30.163 --> 01:02:31.622
He's not my boyfriend.

01:02:32.415 --> 01:02:34.250
Oh. Sorry about that.

01:02:34.333 --> 01:02:36.544
Anyone could've mistaken him
for your boyfriend.

01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:40.047
Then, I'll take it.

01:02:41.132 --> 01:02:43.843
-[elevator dings]
-[door opens]

01:02:45.219 --> 01:02:46.137
Let's go.

01:02:56.731 --> 01:03:01.235
I knew this would be fun,
but I didn't expect it to be so thrilling.

01:03:02.653 --> 01:03:05.865
-What does that mean?
-A "love square" is a first for me.

01:03:07.241 --> 01:03:10.536
That man seemed close to Seok-ryu.

01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:12.538
I'm sorry about earlier.

01:03:13.456 --> 01:03:15.541
You couldn't eat properly because of me.

01:03:16.083 --> 01:03:17.460
It wasn't pleasant.

01:03:18.419 --> 01:03:21.547
The man in front of me had his eyes
at the back of his head.

01:03:21.631 --> 01:03:23.883
Every fiber of his being
was focused on someone else.

01:03:26.135 --> 01:03:27.929
Still, I'll accept your apology.

01:03:29.514 --> 01:03:31.474
Because that will make me look cooler.

01:03:33.351 --> 01:03:34.769
Again, I'm sorry.

01:03:34.852 --> 01:03:36.312
-[phone vibrating]
-[scoffs]

01:03:37.855 --> 01:03:38.898
Just a second.

01:03:41.400 --> 01:03:42.610
Choi Seung-hyo speaking.

01:03:44.278 --> 01:03:46.989
I felt strange today.

01:03:47.782 --> 01:03:50.034
The japchae you made tasted good.

01:03:51.327 --> 01:03:53.955
We sat across from each other
and shared a meal.

01:03:54.622 --> 01:03:56.457
So it felt like old times.

01:03:59.752 --> 01:04:01.796
I'll treat you something
even better next time.

01:04:02.421 --> 01:04:03.631
Hyeon-jun?

01:04:04.590 --> 01:04:05.967
There is no next time.

01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:07.885
It was just this once.

01:04:08.594 --> 01:04:10.304
That's why I agreed to come.

01:04:12.181 --> 01:04:13.099
[clicks tongue]

01:04:13.891 --> 01:04:16.811
Then, let's say this was
the last time we eat steak.

01:04:16.894 --> 01:04:19.897
Next time,
how about pasta for the last time?

01:04:19.981 --> 01:04:24.569
Then, doenjang stew for the last time
and kimchi stew for the last time.

01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:25.736
[Seok-ryu] Hyeon-jun.

01:04:27.321 --> 01:04:28.406
Don't be like this.

01:04:31.367 --> 01:04:32.952
Let's not do this.

01:04:36.247 --> 01:04:37.123
Seok-ryu.

01:04:37.206 --> 01:04:39.750
Can you drop me off
at the nearest station?

01:04:50.553 --> 01:04:51.637
[phone chiming]

01:04:52.513 --> 01:04:54.682
LAVENDER
JAE-SUK, IN-SUK

01:04:54.765 --> 01:04:57.184
-[phone chiming]
-[scoffs]

01:04:57.268 --> 01:04:59.604
Everyone's so quick to respond.

01:05:00.271 --> 01:05:02.481
Did they finally figure out
what day it is today?

01:05:08.654 --> 01:05:10.197
[phone chiming]

01:05:10.281 --> 01:05:11.115
[Jae-suk] Emergency!

01:05:11.198 --> 01:05:13.451
I ordered frozen crabs
and had them sent to my office.

01:05:13.534 --> 01:05:15.077
But I forgot and left to see someone.

01:05:15.161 --> 01:05:18.539
They're all going to spoil.
Can someone put them in their fridge?

01:05:18.623 --> 01:05:22.168
[In-suk] Goodness, I can't help!
I'm so sorry.

01:05:22.251 --> 01:05:24.503
I'm eating out with my family.

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:26.797
[Mi-suk] I have plans too, so I can't go.

01:05:26.881 --> 01:05:29.467
If Hye-suk's off work, can't she go?

01:05:29.550 --> 01:05:30.718
Seriously?

01:05:30.801 --> 01:05:32.261
[amusing music playing]

01:05:32.345 --> 01:05:34.430
These little brats.

01:05:34.513 --> 01:05:37.391
Is melting ice more important
than your friend's birthday?

01:05:39.518 --> 01:05:40.770
[sighs]

01:05:43.272 --> 01:05:44.273
[exhales]

01:05:50.446 --> 01:05:52.406
I'll go.

01:05:59.080 --> 01:05:59.956
[music ends]

01:06:00.998 --> 01:06:01.832
[keys jingling]

01:06:01.916 --> 01:06:04.293
HYEREUNG REALTY

01:06:08.839 --> 01:06:11.300
Why would they asked me to do this?
[grunts]

01:06:12.093 --> 01:06:14.845
Why is this so heavy? Jeez.

01:06:14.929 --> 01:06:16.013
Goodness.

01:06:16.555 --> 01:06:17.682
Damn it!

01:06:17.765 --> 01:06:20.226
-[party popper pops]
-[Hye-suk screams]

01:06:20.309 --> 01:06:21.435
[all laughing]

01:06:21.519 --> 01:06:23.396
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

01:06:23.479 --> 01:06:25.648
[Hye-suk] Hey, what's going on?

01:06:25.731 --> 01:06:27.274
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

01:06:27.358 --> 01:06:28.901
You brats!

01:06:29.652 --> 01:06:31.570
You scared me!

01:06:31.654 --> 01:06:34.407
♪ Happy birthday, dear Hye-suk ♪

01:06:34.490 --> 01:06:36.784
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

01:06:36.867 --> 01:06:38.703
Hey! Blow out your candles!

01:06:38.786 --> 01:06:40.413
Make a wish before you do!

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:42.957
I bad-mouthed all of you so much.
I'm sorry.

01:06:45.042 --> 01:06:47.753
[all cheering]

01:06:49.005 --> 01:06:51.340
Surprise!
You were so surprised, weren't you?

01:06:51.424 --> 01:06:52.967
I really wanted to try this!

01:06:53.050 --> 01:06:55.177
I'd only seen it on TV.
It's my first time!

01:06:55.261 --> 01:06:57.430
It's childish. I tried to stop her.
You don't like…

01:06:58.389 --> 01:07:00.975
I guess she does like it.
She loves this stuff.

01:07:01.058 --> 01:07:05.104
Goodness, who knew we'd live
to see the day when Hye-suk cried?

01:07:05.187 --> 01:07:06.480
I know.

01:07:06.564 --> 01:07:07.940
Hey, Ice Princess.

01:07:08.024 --> 01:07:10.735
It only took 60 years,
but your heart's finally warmed.

01:07:10.818 --> 01:07:13.654
It's because there were too many candles.

01:07:13.738 --> 01:07:16.699
Who would cluelessly put all of these in?

01:07:16.782 --> 01:07:19.368
We didn't go with Korean age,
so we took one out.

01:07:19.452 --> 01:07:20.578
Really?

01:07:20.661 --> 01:07:21.495
[phone chimes]

01:07:22.288 --> 01:07:23.372
[gasps]

01:07:23.456 --> 01:07:24.415
-What?
-Who is it?

01:07:24.498 --> 01:07:25.666
It's Seung-hyo.

01:07:25.750 --> 01:07:27.334
[Seung-hyo] Happy birthday, Mom.

01:07:27.418 --> 01:07:29.378
I left early,
so I didn't get a chance to say.

01:07:29.462 --> 01:07:30.379
[Mi-suk] Must be nice.

01:07:30.463 --> 01:07:33.674
-It is nice. I love it.
-[Jae-suk] What about your husband?

01:07:33.758 --> 01:07:36.969
-Did he prepare anything?
-Hey, birthdays are no big deal.

01:07:37.053 --> 01:07:39.013
He left early for an emergency
this morning.

01:07:39.096 --> 01:07:40.639
Yeah, he's a busy man.

01:07:40.723 --> 01:07:44.060
-Let's cut the cake!
-[Jae-suk] Yeah, let's taste it.

01:07:44.143 --> 01:07:45.603
Is that green tea frosting?

01:07:45.686 --> 01:07:47.354
No, it's mugwort.

01:07:47.438 --> 01:07:48.731
Jeez, I'm so sick of it!

01:07:48.814 --> 01:07:51.901
[In-suk] We're no longer the Suk Sisters!
Why bring that up again?

01:07:51.984 --> 01:07:55.404
[Mi-suk] Hey,
mugwort is good for your health.

01:07:55.488 --> 01:07:58.157
-Bring some plates, Jae-suk.
-[Jae-suk] Okay, are there forks?

01:07:58.240 --> 01:08:00.076
-[Mi-suk] No, we need some.
-Bring everything.

01:08:00.159 --> 01:08:01.619
[indistinct chatter]

01:08:06.916 --> 01:08:08.751
[pleasant music playing]

01:08:11.087 --> 01:08:13.464
Do you have any lily of the valley?

01:08:15.841 --> 01:08:16.926
Hello.

01:08:17.426 --> 01:08:18.719
Do you have lily of the valleys?

01:08:20.304 --> 01:08:21.555
I need lily of the valleys.

01:08:24.975 --> 01:08:26.185
[phone vibrating]

01:08:29.105 --> 01:08:31.065
[Hye-suk] Thank you, my son.

01:08:35.820 --> 01:08:37.947
[Seung-hyo] Oh? Ms. Yu!

01:08:38.030 --> 01:08:39.448
How did you know I was here?

01:08:40.825 --> 01:08:42.159
The other teachers told me.

01:08:42.243 --> 01:08:45.746
They said an unrealistically
handsome young man was at the pool.

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:47.998
I thought it was a water spirit,
so I came.

01:08:48.082 --> 01:08:49.542
[both chuckle]

01:08:50.292 --> 01:08:52.419
Congratulations on winning
the design contest.

01:08:52.503 --> 01:08:55.881
Thank you.
I was surprised to get the call.

01:08:55.965 --> 01:08:58.884
What do you mean?
It went to the rightful winner.

01:09:00.845 --> 01:09:03.305
This place is special to you.

01:09:05.099 --> 01:09:06.267
It is.

01:09:07.643 --> 01:09:09.854
Oh, did you tell Seok-ryu too?

01:09:09.937 --> 01:09:12.857
-No, not yet.
-Hurry and tell her. She'll love it.

01:09:13.524 --> 01:09:14.650
She won't remember.

01:09:14.733 --> 01:09:15.776
Of course, she will.

01:09:15.860 --> 01:09:18.779
She called to ask if the results
were out a few days ago.

01:09:20.322 --> 01:09:22.158
[pleasant music playing]

01:09:22.241 --> 01:09:24.618
Hi, Ms. Yu. It's Seok-ryu.

01:09:25.119 --> 01:09:27.955
Are the results
for Choisseung's contest out yet?

01:09:29.665 --> 01:09:31.208
Not yet?

01:09:31.292 --> 01:09:34.461
Okay. I'm sorry to keep calling you.

01:09:35.045 --> 01:09:36.046
[groans softly]

01:09:45.097 --> 01:09:46.765
Are they out now?

01:09:47.725 --> 01:09:48.601
MINISTRY OF EDUCATION

01:09:48.684 --> 01:09:49.518
ANNOUNCEMENTS

01:09:54.231 --> 01:09:56.609
What's taking so long?

01:09:56.692 --> 01:09:58.152
Hello!

01:09:58.235 --> 01:10:02.531
Are the results of Hyereung High's
gym remodeling and design contest out yet?

01:10:03.949 --> 01:10:05.117
Yes, Hyereung High School.

01:10:06.452 --> 01:10:07.912
Not yet?

01:10:08.954 --> 01:10:10.706
Okay, thank you.

01:10:14.043 --> 01:10:16.795
[Jin-ae] I think she thought
I'd find out sooner.

01:10:16.879 --> 01:10:18.589
She's asked me several times.

01:10:19.298 --> 01:10:20.466
[exhales audibly]

01:10:20.549 --> 01:10:22.176
[exhilarating music playing]

01:10:22.259 --> 01:10:23.469
I'll get going now.

01:10:23.552 --> 01:10:25.804
Have some alone time with the pool.

01:10:27.181 --> 01:10:29.934
You have to create a new future.

01:10:30.017 --> 01:10:32.144
Make sure it's a nice goodbye
to the past.

01:10:35.731 --> 01:10:36.815
Seung-hyo, good luck!

01:10:36.899 --> 01:10:39.109
-[chuckles softly]
-[Jin-ae chuckles] Bye!

01:10:45.658 --> 01:10:48.494
[Tae-hui] No matter
how carefully I shape the clay,

01:10:48.577 --> 01:10:51.330
no one knows
how it'll come out from the fire.

01:10:51.413 --> 01:10:54.041
Will it become a perfectly formed vessel?

01:10:54.124 --> 01:10:58.003
Or will it crack and shatter to pieces?

01:10:59.421 --> 01:11:01.507
You won't know
until it goes in the kiln.

01:11:03.592 --> 01:11:04.426
Seung-hyo,

01:11:04.510 --> 01:11:06.971
you have to save yourself
from unrequited love.

01:11:07.054 --> 01:11:09.014
Even I can't rescue you.

01:11:09.890 --> 01:11:12.643
[Dan-ho] There once was an athlete
in the 200-meter event

01:11:12.726 --> 01:11:15.938
whose weakness was
being slow off the blocks.

01:11:16.021 --> 01:11:19.191
But despite this, he overcame it
through his tireless efforts.

01:11:19.275 --> 01:11:20.901
Even if it's a bit late,

01:11:20.985 --> 01:11:24.446
I'd tell him to muster up the courage,
just like the swimmer did.

01:11:31.996 --> 01:11:32.955
[phone vibrating]

01:11:33.038 --> 01:11:36.583
CHOISSEUNG

01:11:36.667 --> 01:11:37.501
[Seok-ryu] What?

01:11:37.584 --> 01:11:39.837
-Where are you right now?
-[Seok-ryu] Why do you care?

01:11:39.920 --> 01:11:40.921
Where are you?

01:11:41.005 --> 01:11:43.215
I'm at my dad's shop. I'm practicing.

01:11:43.299 --> 01:11:45.134
Wait right there. I'm on my way now.

01:11:45.217 --> 01:11:46.510
[pleasant music playing]

01:12:02.860 --> 01:12:06.196
[Hye-suk] What's this? [chuckles]
Why did you come here?

01:12:07.072 --> 01:12:08.574
[dramatic whoosh]

01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:18.959
[dramatic music playing]

01:12:25.257 --> 01:12:26.383
[breathing heavily]

01:12:26.467 --> 01:12:27.801
[mellow music playing]

01:12:29.136 --> 01:12:33.724
[Seung-hyo] Looking back, I had plenty
of chances to tell her how I felt.

01:12:34.433 --> 01:12:35.976
-[Geun-sik] Smile!
-Honey, me too!

01:12:36.060 --> 01:12:39.104
-[Geun-sik] Get out of there!
-Okay

01:12:39.188 --> 01:12:41.648
-Take it! Smile!
-Okay! One, two, three!

01:12:41.732 --> 01:12:42.858
[camera shutter clicks]

01:12:42.941 --> 01:12:45.069
-[Geun-sik] Okay, now!
-Get out for a second.

01:12:45.152 --> 01:12:47.696
[Seok-ryu] Let's take one together.
Take one of us!

01:12:47.780 --> 01:12:50.574
[Geun-sik] Okay! One, two, three.

01:12:50.657 --> 01:12:52.451
Seung-hyo, take one with Seok-ryu.

01:12:52.534 --> 01:12:54.161
-[Seok-ryu] Yeah.
-No, it's fine.

01:12:54.244 --> 01:12:56.330
-Just take it. Come here.
-[Geun-sik] Hurry up.

01:12:56.413 --> 01:12:57.498
Here we go!

01:12:57.581 --> 01:12:59.541
One, two, three!

01:12:59.625 --> 01:13:01.001
[camera shutter clicks]

01:13:01.085 --> 01:13:04.505
[Seung-hyo] The day we graduated
high school and finally became adults.

01:13:05.005 --> 01:13:06.507
God.

01:13:06.590 --> 01:13:07.716
I can't stand to look.

01:13:08.717 --> 01:13:11.095
-Where are you going dressed like that?
-A date.

01:13:11.762 --> 01:13:13.764
It's a group date with PE majors.

01:13:13.847 --> 01:13:15.599
I hear they're really handsome.

01:13:25.317 --> 01:13:27.027
[Seung-hyo] The day
the ice cream was sweet

01:13:27.945 --> 01:13:31.407
and cherry blossoms flew in spring
when we were immature 20-year-olds.

01:13:34.118 --> 01:13:35.369
Where are you going?

01:13:35.452 --> 01:13:37.246
The US. I found it.

01:13:38.789 --> 01:13:40.707
I got into UC Berkkeley.

01:13:40.791 --> 01:13:43.585
On a full ride too! Isn't it awesome?

01:13:44.169 --> 01:13:47.005
Remember my friend, So-yun?

01:13:47.089 --> 01:13:51.260
She applied,
so I just put in an application too.

01:13:51.343 --> 01:13:52.428
But look!

01:13:52.511 --> 01:13:53.720
I got in.

01:13:56.432 --> 01:14:00.102
They say you follow friends to Gangnam,
but I'm following mine to the US.

01:14:01.395 --> 01:14:04.398
Honestly, I thought
my mom would be against it.

01:14:04.481 --> 01:14:06.316
But she told me to go.

01:14:06.984 --> 01:14:07.818
[coughing]

01:14:07.901 --> 01:14:11.155
[Seok-ryu] But I'm
actually a little excited.

01:14:12.030 --> 01:14:14.533
This will be my first time overseas.

01:14:15.117 --> 01:14:16.952
And it'll be my first time on a plane.

01:14:17.035 --> 01:14:20.414
I've never even been to Jeju.
But my first trip is to the US!

01:14:21.123 --> 01:14:22.499
Isn't this amazing?

01:14:24.918 --> 01:14:28.797
That late night at the tent bar
when she said she was going to the US.

01:14:30.340 --> 01:14:31.550
And…

01:14:32.342 --> 01:14:33.719
-tonight.
-[doorbell chiming]

01:14:34.386 --> 01:14:36.013
-Seok-ryu.
-Hey, right now…

01:14:36.096 --> 01:14:37.890
Hear me out first. [panting]

01:14:40.184 --> 01:14:41.935
I won't delay it any longer.

01:14:42.561 --> 01:14:44.354
I said I'd wait until later,

01:14:45.856 --> 01:14:48.484
but that was an excuse I made
to pretend to be considerate.

01:14:50.110 --> 01:14:51.653
I lied to myself.

01:14:53.780 --> 01:14:56.200
It was out of fear. I was scared.

01:14:57.826 --> 01:14:58.952
So…

01:15:01.330 --> 01:15:02.664
The thing is…

01:15:05.667 --> 01:15:06.877
I'm going to say it this time.

01:15:09.379 --> 01:15:11.423
When I said you were driving me crazy…

01:15:13.425 --> 01:15:15.636
When I said I was losing my mind
because of you…

01:15:16.929 --> 01:15:18.222
What I meant by that was…

01:15:23.018 --> 01:15:24.019
I…

01:15:30.359 --> 01:15:31.401
like you.

01:15:32.569 --> 01:15:34.029
[mellow music playing]

01:15:42.287 --> 01:15:47.167
LOVE IS ALL ABOUT TIMING

01:15:47.251 --> 01:15:52.589
ALREADY LOVE

01:15:52.673 --> 01:15:54.591
[pop song playing]

01:16:25.414 --> 01:16:29.626
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:16:29.710 --> 01:16:31.128
How do I face her tomorrow?

01:16:31.211 --> 01:16:32.838
She's not asleep. No.

01:16:32.921 --> 01:16:36.508
If you've drawn the knife,
you should cut something.

01:16:36.592 --> 01:16:39.052
-Why aren't you in a T-shirt today?
-I washed them.

01:16:39.136 --> 01:16:40.512
[Mi-suk] You wore perfume too?

01:16:41.054 --> 01:16:43.599
Does that mean your answer
has no expiration date?

01:16:44.182 --> 01:16:45.851
Seung-hyo might not know,

01:16:46.435 --> 01:16:48.145
but I think I liked him first.

01:16:48.645 --> 01:16:50.981
[Dan-ho] I want to clear up
any misunderstandings about me.

01:16:51.064 --> 01:16:53.442
Not just anyone can survive
the social affairs department.

01:16:53.525 --> 01:16:55.068
I've changed my strategy.

01:16:55.152 --> 01:16:57.613
The "lasts" didn't work,
so I'm going back to the beginning.

01:16:57.696 --> 01:17:00.449
[Seung-hyo] The reason why I can't stay
as Seok-ryu's friend

01:17:00.532 --> 01:17:01.825
isn't because she's a woman.

01:17:02.409 --> 01:17:03.577
It's because she's Seok-ryu.

01:17:07.122 --> 01:17:10.125
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
